@page "/privacy"
@using Microsoft.Extensions.Options
@inject IOptions<SiteOptions> Site

<PageTitle>Privacy · C# Advent</PageTitle>

<article class="max-w-3xl text-slate-700">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">Last updated October 21, 2026</p>

    <p class="mt-6 text-lg">
        The short version: we collect only what we need to run C# Advent, we never sell it, and we delete contact details after
        each season.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Who we are</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
        C# Advent is a community event run by volunteers. The organizers, Calvin Allen and Matt Groves, are responsible for the
        information on this site. <a href="mailto:@Site.Value.ContactEmail" class="text-advent-700 underline">@Site.Value.ContactEmail</a>
        reaches both of them.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">What we collect</h2>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-3 pl-6">
        <li>
            <strong class="text-slate-900">When you sign in with GitHub:</strong> your GitHub user ID, username and profile name,
            and your primary email address if you've verified it with GitHub. We only ask GitHub for permission to read your
            email addresses, not for access to your repositories or anything else.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong class="text-slate-900">When you claim a spot:</strong> the name and link you want on the calendar, any
            comments for the organizers, and the social media accounts you choose to give us.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong class="text-slate-900">When you join the backup list:</strong> the name and link you'd want on the calendar,
            any notes for the organizers, and, if you fill in for someone, your post's title and address.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong class="text-slate-900">When your entry is on the calendar:</strong> your name, your link, and your post's
            title and address are public, on the calendar, in the archive, and in our posts about it.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong class="text-slate-900">When you visit:</strong> our hosting keeps diagnostic records of requests, such as the
            page, how long it took, and any errors, with an approximate location (country and city). Your IP address is used to
            find that location and then thrown away, not stored.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Cookies</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
        We only use the cookies the site needs to work: one that keeps you signed in, one that protects our forms from forgery,
        and a short-lived one while you sign in with GitHub. There are no analytics, advertising or third-party tracking cookies.
        Our emails don't track whether you open them or click their links.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">How we use it</h2>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-3 pl-6">
        <li>To review claims and put your entry on the calendar.</li>
        <li>
            To email you about C# Advent: that we received or approved your claim, reminders before your day if we don't have your
            post's link yet, and anything else about your spot.
        </li>
        <li>To ask backup posters, one at a time in sign-up order, to fill a spot whose author dropped out or hasn't sent their post.</li>
        <li>
            During Advent, to send everyone with a spot a daily email with the new posts, so they can help share them. Every one of
            those emails has a link that turns them off.
        </li>
        <li>To tag you when we share your post on C# Advent's social media accounts, using only the accounts you gave us.</li>
        <li>To keep the site secure and working.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-3">
        We use your information because you asked to take part, and to keep the site running safely. We never sell or rent it, we
        never use it for advertising, and we only email you about C# Advent.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Who else sees it</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
        The organizers see everything you send us. A few services run the site for us and handle information only to do that:
        Microsoft Azure (hosting, the database, diagnostics, and sending our emails) and GitHub (sign-in).
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">How long we keep it</h2>
    <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-3 pl-6">
        <li>
            <strong class="text-slate-900">Contact details:</strong> on February 1 after each season, we automatically delete
            that season's email addresses, claim requests and comments, and standby list, along with the email address saved
            with your account. The next time you sign in, GitHub gives us your current address again.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong class="text-slate-900">Your account:</strong> your GitHub user ID and username, and any social media accounts
            you gave us, so we can credit your entries and fill in your next claim for you. Ask us and we'll delete them.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong class="text-slate-900">Calendar entries:</strong> kept as part of the archive. Ask us if you'd like yours
            taken down.
        </li>
        <li><strong class="text-slate-900">Diagnostic records:</strong> up to 90 days.</li>
        <li><strong class="text-slate-900">Database backups:</strong> 14 days, so anything we delete is gone from backups after that.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Your choices</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
        Email <a href="mailto:@Site.Value.ContactEmail" class="text-advent-700 underline">@Site.Value.ContactEmail</a> to see,
        correct or delete the information we have about you, or to take down an entry. We'll reply within 30 days. If you're
        unhappy with how we've handled your information, you can also complain to your local data protection authority.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Changes</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
        If we change how we handle information, we'll update this page and the date at the top. See also our
        <a href="terms" class="text-advent-700 underline">terms</a>.
    </p>
</article>
